                        "entry_id": "314eb12e-2d04-39c5-b44a-0d8e4707ea24",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Theory, as opposed to practice."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77731092-e0c2-4a94-a855-641ae4360b62",
                                "sense_id": "ba16472d-92eb-3dc1-a2d8-fafcb5e6d2f9",
                                "text": "So that the art and practic part of life Must be the mistress to this theoric"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c7c6779-00ee-46ea-b04b-cc8bf5481e8e",
                                "sense_id": "ba16472d-92eb-3dc1-a2d8-fafcb5e6d2f9",
                                "text": "We travel into Italie to learne the art of fencing, and practise it at the cost of our lives, before we know it; it were requisite, according to the order of true discipline, we should preferre the theorike before the practike."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf5aee4c-c37d-4fc7-b8d8-0f265197832a",
                                "sense_id": "ba16472d-92eb-3dc1-a2d8-fafcb5e6d2f9",
                                "text": "Jucundus[…]confesseth of himself, that he was mightily delighted with these husbandry studies, and took extraordinary pleasure in them: if the theoric or speculation can so much affect, what shall the place and exercise, the practic part, do?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
